# libretranslate
msgid "**Non-Invasive:** Does not alter the content of `.profile`."
msgstr "**Mitteinvasiivne:** ei muuda `.profile`."

# libretranslate
msgid "**Non-Invasive:** Does not alter the content of ``.profile``."
msgstr "**Mitteinvasiivne:** ei muuda ``.profile``."

# libretranslate
msgid "**Not every subject is a compose project.** Discourse is built by its own `./launcher rebuild` ([handlers/stack_host.yml](../../../web-app-discourse/handlers/stack_host.yml)) and runs as a plain container with no compose label. The drill treats such a container as a subject whenever it mounts a volume this generation backed up: it is stopped with everything else and started again at the end, and its return is asserted like any other. Left running it would take an `rsync --delete` into its live data directory, and the chain's consumer check — which reads compose labels — would not see it, so the dump replay would race it exactly like the zammad failure this whole change came from."
msgstr "**Mitte iga teema ei ole komponeeritud projekt.** Diskursus on ehitatud omaette `./launcher rebuild` ([handlers/stack_host.yml](../../../web-app-discourse/handlers/stack_host.yml)) ja töötab tavalise konteinerina ilma komponeeritud sildita. Puur käsitleb sellist konteinerit subjektina, kui ta paigaldab selle põlvkonna varundatud mahu: see peatatakse kõige muuga ja alustatakse uuesti lõpus ja selle tagastamine kinnitatakse nagu iga teine. Vasakul jooksmine võtaks `rsync --delete` oma live-andmekataloogi ja ahela tarbijakontroll - mis loeb komponeeritud silte - ei näeks seda, nii et prügikasti kordus võistleks see täpselt nagu zammadi ebaõnnestumine, millest kogu muutus tuli."

