# libretranslate
msgid "**Test notes.** The RBAC tiers are proven by moving ``biber`` through the groups with LAM’s Multi edit tool and asserting both the grant and the revoke, rather than by dedicated accounts. ``/ui/vault/logout`` does not end a session — the Ember app restores its token from browser storage — so use the UI’s own logout control when the session must actually be gone."
msgstr "**Testitulemused.** RBAC-tasemeid tõestatakse liikumisega ``biber`` Rühmade kaudu, millel on LAM-i multitöötlusvahend, ja kinnitades nii toetuse kui ka tühistamise, mitte sihtotstarbeliste kontode kaudu. ``/ui/vault/logout`` ei lõpeta seanssi - Emberi rakendus taastab oma märgi brauseri salvestusest - nii et kasutage kasutajaliidese enda väljalogimise juhtimist, kui seanss peab tegelikult olema läinud."

# libretranslate
msgid "**Test notes.** The RBAC tiers are proven by moving `biber` through the groups with LAM's Multi edit tool and asserting both the grant and the revoke, rather than by dedicated accounts. `/ui/vault/logout` does not end a session — the Ember app restores its token from browser storage — so use the UI's own logout control when the session must actually be gone."
msgstr "**Testitulemused.** RBAC-tasemeid tõestatakse liikumisega `biber` LAMi mitme redigeerimisvahendiga rühmade kaudu ja kinnitades nii toetuse kui ka tühistamise, mitte sihtotstarbeliste kontode kaudu. `/ui/vault/logout` ei lõpeta seanssi - Emberi rakendus taastab oma märgi brauseri salvestusest - nii et kasutage kasutajaliidese enda väljalogimise juhtimist, kui seanss peab tegelikult olema läinud."

# libretranslate
msgid "**Testing and documentation tooling.** New *test-e2e-cli* exercises the command-line interface end to end. Lint and test jobs publish per-target and per-test summaries, failed target logs are replayed after the summary, and the complexity matrix shows whether a role already exists on *origin/main*. Generated role READMEs now provide consistent status tables, quick-start instructions and dependency diagrams."
msgstr "**Testimine ja dokumenteerimine.** Uus *test-e2e-klii* kasutab käsurealiidest lõpuni. Lint ja test töökohad avaldavad iga eesmärgi ja testi kokkuvõtted, ebaõnnestunud sihtlogid esitatakse pärast kokkuvõtet uuesti ja keerukuse maatriks näitab, kas roll on juba olemas *päritolu/põhiaine*Loodud roll READMEs pakub nüüd järjepidevaid olekutabeleid, kiire käivitamise juhiseid ja sõltuvuse diagramme."

# libretranslate
msgid "**Tests in every language the project ships.** The quality gate parses each shipped language and runs its unit suite; the PHP and Ruby interpreters are baked into the image, and the JavaScript, PHP and Ruby suites are reported in the CI summary alongside Python. Playwright stages the persona flows once per run and mounts them read-only, and the workspace environment suite splits into base, compose and swarm tracks."
msgstr "**Testid kõigis projekti laevade keeltes.** Kvaliteedivärav sõelub iga saadetud keele ja käivitab selle üksusepaketi; PHP ja Ruby tõlgid küpsetatakse pildile ning JavaScript, PHP ja Ruby sviidid on esitatud CI kokkuvõttes koos Pythoniga. Playwright lavastab persona voolab üks kord jooksu kohta ja paigaldab need kirjutuskaitstult ning tööruumi keskkonnapakett jaguneb baas-, komponeerimis- ja süleradadeks."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The UI is published, the MCP surface is not.** *(Revised during implementation; the original decision was internal-only for both.)* Home Assistant follows the `web-app-*` contract and serves its own UI on a canonical domain through the reverse proxy, because every part of that contract — `meta/domains.yml`, `meta/csp.yml`, the guest Playwright persona — assumes a public vhost, and a role without one would have to be shaped as a `svc-*` role instead. The hub's own auth provider guards that surface. The MCP endpoint stays `exposure: internal`: it is reachable in-cluster only, an unauthenticated probe of the public origin is refused, and `files/playwright/test-mcp-guest.js` asserts exactly that. A platform-SSO gate in front of the UI remains a documented follow-up."
msgstr "**UI on avaldatud, MCP pind mitte.** *(Vaadati läbi rakendamise ajal; esialgne otsus oli ainult asutusesisene mõlema puhul.)* Koduabiline jälgib `web-app-*` sõlmida ja teenindada oma kasutajaliidest kanoonilisel domeenil pöördproksi kaudu, sest selle lepingu iga osa – `meta/domains.yml`, `meta/csp.yml`, külaline Playwright persona - võtab avaliku vhost ja rolli ilma selleta tuleks kujundada kui `svc-*` rolli asemel. Keskuse enda auth pakkuja valvab seda pinda. MCP tulemusnäitaja püsib `exposure: internal`: see on kättesaadav ainult klastrisiseselt, avaliku päritoluga kinnitamata proovivõtturist keeldutakse ja `files/playwright/test-mcp-guest.js` kinnitab täpselt seda. Platvormi-SSO värav kasutajaliidese ees jääb dokumenteeritud järelmeetmeks."

msgid "**The ``mcp`` role is granted per platform, not per application.** A user’s ``roles:`` list carries role names only, and ```build_realm_rbac_groups`` <../web-app-keycloak/filter_plugins/build_realm_rbac_groups.py>`__ matches them without an application context, so ``roles: [mcp]`` makes that user a member of *every* deployed ``/roles/<app>/mcp`` group. Entitling somebody to drive Baserow but not GitLab is therefore not expressible declaratively today; it needs the Keycloak membership to be set directly on the single group. The tool-server side honours whatever membership arrives, so the limit is the platform’s user model, not this wiring, and the Playwright coverage reflects it: it proves “all groups sees all servers” and “no group sees none”, not the selective case."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "**The `mcp` role is granted per platform, not per application.** A user's `roles:` list carries role names only, and [`build_realm_rbac_groups`](../web-app-keycloak/filter_plugins/build_realm_rbac_groups.py) matches them without an application context, so `roles: [mcp]` makes that user a member of *every* deployed `/roles/<app>/mcp` group. Entitling somebody to drive Baserow but not GitLab is therefore not expressible declaratively today; it needs the Keycloak membership to be set directly on the single group. The tool-server side honours whatever membership arrives, so the limit is the platform's user model, not this wiring, and the Playwright coverage reflects it: it proves \"all groups sees all servers\" and \"no group sees none\", not the selective case."
msgstr "**Theo `mcp` roll on antud platvormi, mitte taotluse kohta.** Kasutaja oma `roles:` nimekiri kannab ainult rollinimesid ja [`build_realm_rbac_groups`](../web-app-keycloak/filter_plugins/build_realm_rbac_groups.py) sobib ilma rakenduse kontekstita, nii et `roles: [mcp]` muudab selle kasutaja *iga* saadeti `/roles/<app>/mcp` grupi. Seega ei ole õigus juhtida Baserow'd, kuid mitte GitLabi, täna deklaratiivselt väljendatav; see vajab Keycloaki liikmelisuse määramist otse ühele rühmale. Tööriista-serveri pool austab mis tahes liikmelisust, nii et piirang on platvormi kasutajamudel, mitte see juhtmestik, ja Playwrighti katvus peegeldab seda: see tõestab \"kõik grupid näevad kõiki servereid\" ja \"ükski grupp ei näe\", mitte valikuline juhtum."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The agent then runs autonomously, step by step:**"
msgstr "**Seejärel töötab agent iseseisvalt, samm-sammult:**"

# libretranslate
msgid "**The app volumes are really discarded** (`down --volumes`) and re-created empty by `compose create`, so what comes back can only come from the backup. The database projects go down without `--volumes` on purpose: their data directory carries the database itself, which the deploy creates and the container does not, so a wiped datadir would leave `baudolo-restore --empty -d <db>` with nothing to connect to. The database half loses no proof by it — the pre-clean drops the schema including the marker table, and only the dump brings it back."
msgstr "**Rakenduse mahud on tõesti kõrvale jäetud** (`down --volumes`) ja taasloodud tühjalt `compose create`, See, mis tuleb tagasi, saab tulla ainult tagavarast. Andmebaasi projektid lähevad alla ilma `--volumes` eesmärgipäraselt: nende andmekataloog kannab andmebaasi ise, mille juurutamine loob ja konteiner seda ei tee, nii et pühkitud andmekast lahkuks `baudolo-restore --empty -d <db>` pole millegagi ühenduses olla. Andmebaasi pool ei kaota selle abil mingit tõestust - eelnevalt puhas langeb skeem, sealhulgas markerlaud, ja ainult prügikast toob selle tagasi."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The axes are part of a row's identity.** They appear in the job label as glyphs, in the plan table as columns, and in the artifact name. Two rows that differ only in distro are two deploys and MUST NOT share an artifact name."
msgstr "**Kirved on osa rea identiteedist.** Need esinevad töö sildil glüüfidena, plaanitabelis veergudena ja artefakti nimes. Kaks rida, mis erinevad ainult distros, on kaks juurutamist ja EI TOHI jagada artefakti nime."

# libretranslate
#, python-format
msgid "**The axes are selectable.** `%distro` and `/filesystem` narrow a `whitelist` or `priority` token the same way `@mode` and `+tor` do. A retrigger reads the distro back off a failed job's title, so a red row returns on the distribution it died on. It does not read the filesystem back: the title states the kind the matrix assigned, which a deploy may have fallen back from, and writing it into a token would state it as named by a human and make it binding."
msgstr "**Telgesid saab valida.** `%distro` ja `/filesystem` kitsendada `whitelist` või `priority` samamoodi `@mode` ja `+tor` tee. Retrigger loeb distro tagasi ebaõnnestunud töö pealkirjast, nii et punane rida naaseb jaotusele, kus see suri. See ei loe failisüsteemi tagasi: pealkiri ütleb, millist maatriksit omistatakse, millest juurutamine võib olla tagasi langenud, ja selle kirjutamine märgiks, et see on inimese poolt nimetatud ja muudab selle siduvaks."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The consumers must be down.** `--empty` pre-cleans the schema in one psql session and replays in the next; a booting consumer recreates the schema in between and the dump's own `CREATE TABLE` then fails. The replay checks the consumer's compose project and refuses while anything of it runs."
msgstr "**Tarbijad peavad olema maas.** `--empty` eelpuhastab skeemi ühes psql seansis ja kordus järgmises; alglaadimise tarbija loob uuesti skeemi vahel ja prügimäe enda `CREATE TABLE` siis ebaõnnestub. Kordus kontrollib tarbija komponeerimisprojekti ja keeldub, kui see töötab."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The consumers must be down.** ``--empty`` pre-cleans the schema in one psql session and replays in the next; a booting consumer recreates the schema in between and the dump’s own ``CREATE TABLE`` then fails. The replay checks the consumer’s compose project and refuses while anything of it runs."
msgstr "**Tarbijad peavad olema maas.** ``--empty`` eelpuhastab skeemi ühes psql-seansis ja kordus järgmises; alglaadimise tarbija loob uuesti skeemi vahel ja prügimäe enda. ``CREATE TABLE`` siis ebaõnnestub. Kordus kontrollib tarbija komponeerimisprojekti ja keeldub, kui see töötab."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The deploy can create a role-internal administrator.** On an instance with no users at all there is no OIDC administrator to borrow an API key from, so [`tasks/utils/mcp.yml`](./tasks/utils/mcp.yml) creates the `openwebui-api-bot` declared in [`meta/users.yml`](./meta/users.yml), whose password the platform generates with every other user's. It is deliberately not an OIDC identity: Open WebUI ships `OAUTH_MERGE_ACCOUNTS_BY_EMAIL` disabled and refuses an OIDC login whose email a local account already holds, so seeding a person's address would lock them out of their own login. On an instance that already has an administrator no account is created."
msgstr "**Paigaldamine võib luua rollisisese administraatori.** Juhul, kui kasutajaid pole üldse, ei ole OIDC-administraatorit API võtme laenamiseks, nii et [`tasks/utils/mcp.yml`](./tasks/utils/mcp.yml) loob `openwebui-api-bot` kuulutatud [`meta/users.yml`](./meta/users.yml), kelle parooli platvorm loob iga teise kasutajaga. See ei ole teadlikult OIDC identiteet: Open WebUI laevad `OAUTH_MERGE_ACCOUNTS_BY_EMAIL` keelab ja keeldub OIDC-i sisselogimisest, mille e-posti aadress on juba kohaliku konto käes, nii et isiku aadressi külvamine lukustaks nad oma sisselogimisest välja. Juhul, kui administraator on juba olemas, kontot ei looda."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The deploy can create a role-internal administrator.** On an instance with no users at all there is no OIDC administrator to borrow an API key from, so ```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ creates the ``openwebui-api-bot`` declared in ```meta/users.yml`` <./meta/users.yml>`__, whose password the platform generates with every other user’s. It is deliberately not an OIDC identity: Open WebUI ships ``OAUTH_MERGE_ACCOUNTS_BY_EMAIL`` disabled and refuses an OIDC login whose email a local account already holds, so seeding a person’s address would lock them out of their own login. On an instance that already has an administrator no account is created."
msgstr "**Paigaldamine võib luua rollisisese administraatori.** Juhul, kui kasutajaid pole üldse, ei ole OIDC-administraatorit API võtme laenamiseks, nii et ```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ creates the ``openwebui-api-bot`` declared in ```meta/users.yml`` <./meta/users.yml>`__, whose password the platform generates with every other user’s. It is deliberately not an OIDC identity: Open WebUI ships ``OAUTH_MERGE_ACCOUNTS_BY_EMAIL`` keelab ja keeldub OIDC-i sisselogimisest, mille e-posti aadress on juba kohaliku konto käes, nii et inimese aadressi külvamine lukustaks nad oma sisselogimisest välja. Juhul, kui administraator on juba olemas, kontot ei looda."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The engine is read, not guessed.** It comes from the service key in the consuming role's `meta/services.yml`, the same value that fed the backup seed, resolved through `utils/recovery/databases.py`. A dump whose engine no role claims aborts the run instead of being replayed with an assumption."
msgstr "**Mootorit loetakse, mitte ei arvata.** See pärineb tarbiva rolli teenindusvõtmest `meta/services.yml`, sama väärtus, mis toitis varukoopia seemet, lahendati `utils/recovery/databases.py`. Prügikast, mille mootor ei nõua mingit rolli, katkestab jooksu, selle asemel et seda eeldusega uuesti esitada."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The engine is read, not guessed.** It comes from the service key in the consuming role’s ``meta/services.yml``, the same value that fed the backup seed, resolved through ``utils/recovery/databases.py``. A dump whose engine no role claims aborts the run instead of being replayed with an assumption."
msgstr "**Mootorit loetakse, mitte ei arvata.** See pärineb teenindusvõtmest tarbivas rollis ``meta/services.yml``, sama väärtus, mis toitis varukoopia seemet, lahendati ``utils/recovery/databases.py``. Prügikast, mille mootor ei nõua mingit rolli, katkestab jooksu, selle asemel et seda eeldusega uuesti esitada."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The file's content IS the value of `applications.<app>.<topic>`. There is NO wrapping key matching the filename.**"
msgstr "**Faili sisu ON faili väärtus `applications.<app>.<topic>`. Failinimele vastavat mähkimisvõtit ei ole.**"

# libretranslate
msgid "**The gateway is authenticated with per-consumer virtual keys.** LiteLLM virtual keys are issued per consumer (OpenWebUI, Flowise, and each 032 agent); a master key is admin-only. This gives per-consumer rate limiting and revocation. The gateway MUST NOT be reachable unauthenticated even on the internal overlay. Keys live in each consumer role's `meta/secrets.yml` `credentials:` block."
msgstr "**Värav on autenditud tarbija virtuaalsete võtmetega.** LiteLLM virtuaalvõtmeid väljastatakse tarbija kohta (OpenWebUI, Flowise ja igaüks 032 agent); peavõti on ainult haldusvõti. See annab tarbijale määra piiramise ja tühistamise. Värav ei tohi olla autentimata kättesaadav isegi sisemisel kattel. Võtmed elavad igas tarbijarollis `meta/secrets.yml` `credentials:` blokk."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The head leads unless an operator says otherwise.** Chunk 0 starts at the top of the ranking. The list is ordered coverage-first, so its head is what a run most needs proven, and a sweep that cannot afford the whole list leaves the tail behind rather than sliding a window over it."
msgstr "**Pea juhib, kui operaator ei ütle teisiti.** Chunk 0 Algab edetabeli tipust. Nimekiri on järjestatud katvus-esimene, nii et selle pea on see, mida jooksu kõige vajab tõestatud, ja pühkimine, mis ei saa endale lubada kogu nimekirja jätab saba taha, mitte libisemine aken üle selle."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The integration matrix is a generated artifact with a sanctioned generator.** The generator lives under `cli/build/docs/integration_matrix/` and runs through `make integration-matrix`; `docs/` holds only the rendered page. It MUST satisfy the repo lints: its `EDGES` data moves into a sibling data module so the entrypoint stays under the 500-line limit, it uses the shared project-root helper instead of a local `__file__` upward walk, and it carries no self-path literal or `requirement NNN` token. The generated `027-integration-matrix.md` carries a `generated-artifact / not-a-requirement` head marker so the requirements-completeness/archival lint skips it. Dead upstream URLs in `EDGES` are fixed or dropped on regeneration."
msgstr "**Integratsioonimaatriks on sanktsioneeritud generaatoriga genereeritud artefakt.** Generaator elab all `cli/build/docs/integration_matrix/` ja jookseb läbi `make integration-matrix`; `docs/` hoiab ainult renderdatud lehekülge. See peab rahuldama repo lants: `EDGES` andmed liiguvad õe-venna andmemoodulisse, nii et sisendpunkt jääb alla 500- line limit, see kasutab jagatud projekti-root abistaja asemel kohalikku `__file__` ülespoole kõndimine ja see ei kanna eneseteadlikku ega `requirement NNN` žetoon. Tekkinud `027-integration-matrix.md` kannab `generated-artifact / not-a-requirement` peamarker, nii et nõuete täielikkus/arhiiv jätab selle vahele. Ülesvoolu surnud URL- id `EDGES` on fikseeritud või regenereeritud."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The integration matrix is the cross-role addon backlog.** The full role×role capability map lives in the generated companion [027-integration-matrix.md](027-integration-matrix.md) (source of truth: [cli/build/docs/integration_matrix](../../cli/build/docs/integration_matrix/__main__.py)). ☑️ cells are integrations **already wired** through an infinito-native service flag in the row role's `meta/services.yml` (e.g. `sso`→keycloak, `matomo`, `prometheus`, `email`→mailu), derived by scanning the repo, no action required. ✅ cells are verified **upstream app↔app plugins not yet declared** as addons, the backlog this requirement commits to wire. 🪙 cells are the same as ✅ but gated behind a commercial tier (opt-in, operator-enabled). ❌ cells have no known integration. The matrix MUST be regenerated (not hand-edited) whenever a role or an integration is added; the `meta/addons/` migrations turn ✅ into ☑️ over time."
msgstr "**Integratsioonimaatriks on rollide lisamise mahajäämus.** Täisroll×rollivõime kaart elab loodud kaaslases [027-integratsioon...matrix.md](027-integration-matrix.md) (tõeallikas: [cli/build/docs/integration_matrix](../../cli/build/docs/integration_matrix/__main__.py)).◻️ rakud on integratsioonid **traadiga** Infinito-emakeelse teenuse lipu kaudu rearollis `meta/services.yml` (nt. `sso`→keycloak, `matomo`, `prometheus`, `email`→mailu), mis on saadud repo skaneerimise teel, ei ole vaja midagi teha. ✅ lahtrid on kontrollitud **Upstream app↔app pluginad pole veel deklareeritud** Lisanditena seob see nõue mahajäämuse traadiga. 🪙 rakud on samad, mis ✅, kuid suletud kaubandusliku tasandi taha (opt-in, operator-toega)Rakkudel puudub teadaolev integratsioon. Maatriks PEAB olema regenereeritud (käsitsi redigeerimata) rolli või integratsiooni lisamise korral; `meta/addons/` Migratsioonid muutuvad aja jooksul ̈️."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The job proves the machine before it deploys.** [assert_architecture.sh](../../../scripts/github/runner/assert_architecture.sh) compares `uname -m` against the assigned value and fails the row on a mismatch. Without it, a label that stops resolving to arm64 hardware would report every arm64 row green from an amd64 machine, which is the exact failure the axis exists to rule out."
msgstr "**Töö tõestab masinat enne selle käivitamist.** [assert_architecture.sh](../../../scripts/github/runner/assert_architecture.sh) võrdleb `uname -m` määratud väärtuse suhtes ja ebaõnnestub ebakõla real. Ilma selleta on silt, mis lõpetab käelahutuse64 riistvara annab teada igast käest64 rida roheline amd64 Masin, mis on täpne tõrge, mida telg on olemas, et välistada."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The matrix carries the runner label, and `runs-on` reads it.** The entry gains `architecture` and `runner`; [pools.py](../../../utils/github/variant/pools.py) owns the mapping (`amd64` → `ubuntu-latest`, `arm64` → `ubuntu-24.04-arm`). An architecture without a label is a build error rather than a row that lands on the wrong hardware with an empty `runs-on`."
msgstr "**Maatriks kannab jooksja silti ja `runs-on` loeb.** Sissepääs kasum `architecture` ja `runner`; [pools.py](../../../utils/github/variant/pools.py) omab kaardistamist (`amd64` → `ubuntu-latest`, `arm64` → `ubuntu-24.04-arm`)Sildita arhitektuur on pigem ehitusviga kui rida, mis maandub tühja riistvaraga valele riistvarale `runs-on`."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The migration is blocked on a transport gap, and the credential half of it is already built.** The adapter presented its upstream credential only as a header (`ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_KEY` → `Authorization: Bearer …`) while Baserow keys its endpoint by URL segment, so `policy.upstream_url` now splices an optional `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_PATH_KEY` and `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_PATH_SUFFIX` into the upstream URL, delivered through the same `upstream.env` file. With neither variable set it returns the base URL unchanged, which is why the fourteen existing providers are untouched."
msgstr "**Migratsioon on blokeeritud transpordilüngale ja sellest pool mandaati on juba ehitatud.** Adapter esitas oma ülesvoolu mandaadi ainult päisena (`ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_KEY` → `Authorization: Bearer …`) Kui Baserow klahvib oma lõpp-punkti URL-segmendi järgi, siis `policy.upstream_url` splaissimine `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_PATH_KEY` ja `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_PATH_SUFFIX` ülesvoolu URL-i, mis edastatakse sama kaudu `upstream.env` fail. Kummagi muutujaga ei tagastata baas-URL-i muutmata kujul, mistõttu on neliteist olemasolevat pakkujat puutumata."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The pools are narrowable per run.** The `distros` and `filesystem` inputs default to empty, which means every declared value. Narrowing is for chasing one distribution or one filesystem."
msgstr "**Basseinid on ühe jooksu kohta kitsad.** Theo `distros` ja `filesystem` Sisestab vaikimisi tühjaks, mis tähendab iga deklareeritud väärtust. Kitsendamine on ühe distributsiooni või ühe failisüsteemi jälitamine."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The raft volume is `nfs: false` and the service carries `placement: manager`.**"
msgstr "**Parve maht on `nfs: false` ja teenistus kannab `placement: manager`.**"

# libretranslate
msgid "**The recovery key is the way back in.** ``bao operator init`` issues it once and nothing reissues it, which is what makes it useful — it is the only authority here that does not rotate. It is persisted through ``sys-token-store`` (``DIR_SECRETS``, backed up, and it survives both ``MODE_RESET`` and a replaced manager, each of which takes ``.applied.json`` with it). When neither the inventory AppRole nor the recorded one is accepted, ``tasks/utils/recover.yml`` mints a root token from it and re-pins the AppRole. It cannot decrypt the store — only the seal key can — so it is not a substitute for backing up the inventory."
msgstr "**Taastamise võti on tagasitee sisse.** ``bao operator init`` annab selle välja üks kord ja miski ei anna seda uuesti välja, mis teeb selle kasulikuks - see on siin ainus autoriteet, mis ei roteeru. Seda jätkatakse ``sys-token-store`` (``DIR_SECRETS``, tagurpidi ja see jääb ellu mõlemad ``MODE_RESET`` ja asendatud juhataja, kellest igaüks võtab ``.applied.json`` sellega). Kui ei ole vastu võetud ei inventarinimestikku ega registreeritud inventarinimestikku, ``tasks/utils/recover.yml`` vermib sellest juurmärgi ja taastab AppRole'i. See ei saa kauplust lahti krüptida - ainult pitserivõti saab - nii et see ei asenda varude varundamist."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The recovery key is the way back in.** `bao operator init` issues it once and nothing reissues it, which is what makes it useful — it is the only authority here that does not rotate. It is persisted through `sys-token-store` (`DIR_SECRETS`, backed up, and it survives both `MODE_RESET` and a replaced manager, each of which takes `.applied.json` with it). When neither the inventory AppRole nor the recorded one is accepted, `tasks/utils/recover.yml` mints a root token from it and re-pins the AppRole. It cannot decrypt the store — only the seal key can — so it is not a substitute for backing up the inventory."
msgstr "**Taastamise võti on tagasitee sisse.** `bao operator init` annab selle välja üks kord ja miski ei anna seda uuesti välja, mis teeb selle kasulikuks - see on siin ainus autoriteet, mis ei roteeru. Seda jätkatakse `sys-token-store` (`DIR_SECRETS`, tagurpidi ja see jääb ellu mõlemad `MODE_RESET` ja asendatud juhataja, kellest igaüks võtab `.applied.json` sellega). Kui ei ole vastu võetud ei inventarinimestikku ega registreeritud inventarinimestikku, `tasks/utils/recover.yml` vermib sellest juurmärgi ja taastab AppRole'i. See ei saa kauplust lahti krüptida - ainult pitserivõti saab - nii et see ei asenda varude varundamist."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The role tree is the audit.** Every fact about a role's MCP surface lives in its own `meta/services.yml`; no separate artifact duplicates it."
msgstr "**Rollipuu on audit.** Iga fakt rolli MCP pinna kohta elab omaette `meta/services.yml`; Ükski eraldi artefakt ei dubleeri seda."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The runtime identity differs.** act sets `ACT=true`, so `detect_gha_act()` in [runtime.py](../../../../utils/env/runtime.py) resolves `INFINITO_RUNNING_ON_GITHUB=false` where a real runner resolves `true`. Anything keyed off that fact behaves differently, and act cannot prove a fix to it either way."
msgstr "**Käitamisaja identiteet on erinev.** aktikomplektid `ACT=true`, nii `detect_gha_act()` sisse [runtime.py](../../../../utils/env/runtime.py) lahendab `INFINITO_RUNNING_ON_GITHUB=false` kus tõeline jooksja lahendab `true`. Kõik, mis on selle fakti äravõtnud, käitub teistmoodi ja tegu ei saa sellele kummalgi moel kinnitust leida."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The seal key is the whole ballgame.** The ``static`` seal wraps the raft root key with ``secrets.credentials.seal_key``, injected as ``env://OPENBAO_SEAL_KEY``. A backup of the raft volume is **undecryptable without it**, and ``svc-bkp-secrets-2-local`` does not cover it — the encrypted inventory is its only home, so back the inventory up accordingly. It is pinned ``rotatable: false``: the static seal carries one generation of slack, and spending that every deploy makes any skipped generation unrecoverable. Rotate it deliberately by changing the inventory value; ``openbao.hcl.j2`` then emits the ``previous_key``/``previous_key_id`` pair, the node unseals with the old key and rewraps to the new one."
msgstr "**Hülgevõti on kogu pallimäng.** Theo ``static`` tihend mähkib parve juurklahvi ``secrets.credentials.seal_key``, süstitud ``env://OPENBAO_SEAL_KEY``. Parve mahu varukoopia on **dekrüpteerimata ilma selleta**ja ``svc-bkp-secrets-2-local`` ei kata seda - krüpteeritud inventar on selle ainus kodu, nii et varundage inventuur vastavalt. See on kinnitatud ``rotatable: false``: Staatiline pitser kannab endas ühe põlvkonna lõtvust ja iga kasutuskulu muudab iga vahelejäänud põlvkonna taastumatuks. Pöörata seda teadlikult, muutes varude väärtust; ``openbao.hcl.j2`` kiirgab ``previous_key``/``previous_key_id`` Paar, sõlm avaneb vana võtmega ja pakendab uue."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The seal key is the whole ballgame.** The `static` seal wraps the raft root key with `secrets.credentials.seal_key`, injected as `env://OPENBAO_SEAL_KEY`. A backup of the raft volume is **undecryptable without it**, and `svc-bkp-secrets-2-local` does not cover it — the encrypted inventory is its only home, so back the inventory up accordingly. It is pinned `rotatable: false`: the static seal carries one generation of slack, and spending that every deploy makes any skipped generation unrecoverable. Rotate it deliberately by changing the inventory value; `openbao.hcl.j2` then emits the `previous_key`/`previous_key_id` pair, the node unseals with the old key and rewraps to the new one."
msgstr "**Hülgevõti on kogu pallimäng.** Theo `static` tihend mähkib parve juurklahvi `secrets.credentials.seal_key`, süstitud `env://OPENBAO_SEAL_KEY`. Parve mahu varukoopia on **dekrüpteerimata ilma selleta**ja `svc-bkp-secrets-2-local` ei kata seda - krüpteeritud inventar on selle ainus kodu, nii et varundage inventuur vastavalt. See on kinnitatud `rotatable: false`: Staatiline pitser kannab endas ühe põlvkonna lõtvust ja iga kasutuskulu muudab iga vahelejäänud põlvkonna taastumatuks. Pöörata seda teadlikult, muutes varude väärtust; `openbao.hcl.j2` kiirgab `previous_key`/`previous_key_id` Paar, sõlm avaneb vana võtmega ja pakendab uue."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The version has to fit.** The dump states which server it came out of, in its own header — `-- Dumped from database version 17.11` for postgres, `-- Server version\\t11.8.8-MariaDB` for mariadb. That is compared against the running engine before the pre-clean touches anything. Restoring forward across a major version is the upgrade path and stays allowed; backward is refused, because a newer dump uses syntax an older server rejects and the schema would already be dropped by then. The version is deliberately not kept in `databases.csv`: that file is written at seed time and would state the version deployed back then, not the one the dump came from — and a generation copied to another host carries its header along, a csv row does not."
msgstr "**Versioon peab sobima.** Prügila ütleb, millisest serverist see välja tuli, oma päises - `-- Dumped from database version 17.11` postgresiks, `-- Server version\\t11.8.8-MariaDB` Mariadbile. Seda võrreldakse töötava mootoriga enne, kui eelpuhastamine midagi puudutab. Põhiversiooni edasine taastamine on uuendustee ja jääb lubatud; tagasi lükatakse, sest uuem prügikast kasutab süntaksit, mille vanem server tagasi lükkab ja skeem oleks selleks ajaks juba langenud. Seda versiooni ei säilitata tahtlikult `databases.csv`: see fail on kirjutatud seemne ajal ja selles oleks märgitud toona kasutatud versioon, mitte see, kust prügikast tuli - ja teisele hostile kopeeritud põlvkond kannab oma päist mööda, csv rida ei ole."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The version has to fit.** The dump states which server it came out of, in its own header — ``-- Dumped from database version 17.11`` for postgres, ``-- Server version\\t11.8.8-MariaDB`` for mariadb. That is compared against the running engine before the pre-clean touches anything. Restoring forward across a major version is the upgrade path and stays allowed; backward is refused, because a newer dump uses syntax an older server rejects and the schema would already be dropped by then. The version is deliberately not kept in ``databases.csv``: that file is written at seed time and would state the version deployed back then, not the one the dump came from — and a generation copied to another host carries its header along, a csv row does not."
msgstr "**Versioon peab sobima.** Prügila ütleb, millisest serverist see välja tuli, oma päises - ``-- Dumped from database version 17.11`` postgresiks, ``-- Server version\\t11.8.8-MariaDB`` Mariadbile. Seda võrreldakse töötava mootoriga enne, kui eelpuhastamine midagi puudutab. Põhiversiooni edasine taastamine on uuendustee ja jääb lubatud; tagasi lükatakse, sest uuem prügikast kasutab süntaksit, mille vanem server tagasi lükkab ja skeem oleks selleks ajaks juba langenud. Seda versiooni ei säilitata tahtlikult ``databases.csv``: see fail on kirjutatud seemne ajal ja selles oleks märgitud toona kasutatud versioon, mitte see, kust prügikast tuli - ja teisele hostile kopeeritud põlvkond kannab oma päist mööda, csv rida ei ole."

